{"id":"local-primary","experiment":4,"title":"All 42 primary conditional-law checks","description":"All 42 primary checks meet their finite practical margins. Secondary failures, inconclusive tests and insufficient support are preserved. TV is a nonnegative distance, not a signed difference.","sourcePath":"docs/experiments/local-causal-structure-v1/conditional.csv","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/raghammer1/causal-spacetime-lab/blob/9bc5984c656271c247354e0079fd900702642064/docs/experiments/local-causal-structure-v1/conditional.csv","sha256":"99fe9556088eecf3c1e1d1fa44df0afc7d64f802d587ac86b5ce0120a501011b","columns":["centered_ci95","ci95","count","difference","dimension","estimate","estimate_ci95","family","fit","fit_count","fit_difference_sd","interval_size","mean_centered_count_per_pair","metric","parent_count","reference","reference_ci95","reference_dimension","scope","status","tolerance","undefined_bootstrap_draws","ci_low","ci_high"],"chart":{"x":"metric","y":"difference","low":"ci_low","high":"ci_high","series":"family","reference":0,"referenceLabel":"Exact agreement / zero TV","label":"Reference difference / TV","unit":"probability units"},"defaultFilters":{"family":"slab","dimension":4},"uncertainty":"Pointwise 95% hierarchical percentile intervals, resampling parents and independent references; 2,000 draws. TV bootstrap bias near zero can put the interval above its point estimate; this does not establish a positive distance floor.","sampleUnit":"Three fits; 200 parents per ordinary fit. Intervals within a parent are dependent. Ratios pool counts within each fit and then average fits equally.","assumptions":"Conditional diamond law assumes uniform sampling in a causally convex flat region. Boxes may clip intervals. Support requires ≥30 positive parents and ≥100 intervals in every fit.","selection":"Across-fits N=256 diamond/slab rows, generating dimension equals reference dimension, seven registered observables; exactly 42 rows. Existing interval fields are